commit 5bc4590848032f21c0322896121f366bc0fa85fa
Author: Burak Emre Kabakcı <emrekabakci@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jul 28 17:44:00 2026 +0100

    fix(server): reply with an unlinked notice on non-Slack platforms instead of dropping (#2257)

    * fix(server): reply with an unlinked notice on non-Slack platforms instead of dropping

    An inbound chat message or button click that resolved to no agent (no
    owning agent on the connection, no channel Behavior) was logged and
    dropped. Slack replied via workspaceUnlinkedNotice(); Telegram and every
    other platform gave the user silence with no indication of what was
    wrong or how to fix it.

    workspaceUnlinkedNotice() now returns a generic dashboard+CLI notice for
    non-Slack platforms — no workspace/team deep links, no mrkdwn, and
    deliberately static so no lookup failure can turn the reply back into a
    dead drop. Slack output is unchanged. Both drop sites (the message path
    and ingestClick) now share one postUnlinkedChatNotice() helper, so Slack
    interactions get the notice too; they previously dropped silently.

    Same class, found while there: the notice tells the user to paste
    `/link <code>` into the chat, but on non-Slack platforms that arrives as
    plain message text and died in the same dead end before the dispatcher
    saw it. Slack's `/lobu link` rides the native onSlashCommand ingress and
    was immune. The unrouted path now tries tryHandleSlashText first.

    Loop prevention mirrors the existing Slack semantics with no new state:
    the Chat SDK never re-delivers the bot's own posts (isMe), and a channel
    with a Behavior subscription never reaches the dead end because the
    planner-rejection guard drops it silently first.

    Fixes #2230

    * fix(server): dispatch unrouted slash commands on mention-stripped text

    * fix(server): escape bot user id before building mention-strip regexes

